<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Innovation vs. Templates: Believing that using a pre-existing template (e.g., a simple web template) is acceptable. Innovation and modification must be explicitly documented.</li>
        <li>Teacher Debugging: Expecting the teacher to write or debug the source code. Teachers must remain as advisors, not co-developers.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

